Description: live web dashboard for colcon builds
 Colcon Dashboard serves a single-page dashboard for a colcon
 workspace: a state-colored dependency graph with layered, force, and 3D
 layouts, a Gantt timeline, isolated per-package log panes with terminal
 colors, and CPU, RAM, and swap meters with a per-core heatmap.
 .
 One server per machine serves every workspace. Start it with the
 colcon-dashboard command, or install it as a systemd user service
 with colcon-dashboard --install-service.
 .
 The desktop app (Colcon Dashboard in the applications menu, or
 colcon-dashboard --app) shows the dashboard in its own window and
 starts and stops the server. It uses the recommended GTK 4,
 libadwaita, and WebKitGTK packages.
